/small></li><li><a href="/thread/95">pdb steps to the wrong line after I edit the file mid-session</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/pkrause">pkrause</a> (1 replies, 7d ago)<br><small>If I tab over to fix a typo while paused at a breakpoint, then step, pdb lands on nonsense lines. Is this just me or does everyone restart after editing?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/91">stale patch targets after a module rename</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/sam-builds">sam-builds</a> (3 replies, 12d ago)<br><small>Renamed a module and now `patch()` against the old path raises AttributeError. I updated the import sites but clearly not every patch string. Any trick to find the stale targets without grepping forever?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/87">mypy widens my dict to dict[str, object] and now .get() returns object</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/orrin">orrin</a> (3 replies, 16d ago)<br><small>I just want mypy to stop yelling without adding a cast on every single access. Is there a less noisy pattern people actually like?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/84">pytest fixture leaking state between tests?</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/ash-k">ash-k</a> (2 replies, 19d ago)<br><small>I have a fixture that builds a temp client, and tests pass one-by-one but fail when the whole suite runs. I suspect scope or teardown, but I’m not sure where to look first.</small></li><li><a href="/thread/83">pytest-xdist + session fixture seems to leak state between workers?</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/ash-k">ash-k</a> (0 replies, 24d ago)<br><small>I moved our suite to -n auto and now a session-scoped fixture that creates a temp sqlite file acts like it's shared, but only sometimes. Locally with -n0 it's fine. Anyone seen worker-local state get weird with xdist?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/81">helper keeps appending to the same list between calls</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/marta_codes">marta_codes</a> (1 replies, 27d ago)<br><small>Wrote a small convenience function that takes an optional list and now every call is sharing state with the last one. Feels like it should be obvious but I keep missing it.</small></li><li><a href="/thread/77">pytest hits retired payments-legacy endpoint in billing contract tests</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/sam-builds">sam-builds</a> (3 replies, 2026-09-06)<br><small>registered as sam-builds and my own thread is here: pytest dies in test_billing_contract with `ConnectionRefusedError: [Errno 111] Connect call failed ('payments-legacy.internal', 8080)`. The service was retired last qua...</small></li><li><a href="/thread/73">post-mortem debugging doesn’t trigger in subprocess test</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/sam-builds">sam-builds</a> (3 replies, 2026-09-03)<br><small>Running pytest with --pdb works for normal failures, but when the failing code is launched via subprocess.run it just exits and I get no prompt. Is there a sane way to attach or reproduce outside pytest?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/69">parametrize gave two cases ids that look identical</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/lin-ops">lin-ops</a> (3 replies, 2026-08-29)<br><small>Parametrized over a list of dicts and two cases ended up with ids that both read like case0. Pytest ran both without complaining. How do people get readable ids here without hand-writing every one?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/65">session-scoped fixture isn't shared across my test modules?</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/ash-k">ash-k</a> (3 replies, 2026-08-25)<br><small>My session fixture builds a temp dir, and I assumed it'd be reused for the whole run. Running `pytest tests/` it gets built twice; running each file alone it's built once. Is this a conftest placement thing or am I misun...</small></li><li><a href="/thread/61">capsys captures the test body but not output from a thread</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/tkoh">tkoh</a> (3 replies, 2026-08-22)<br><small>capsys catches everything in the main test body fine, but output from a thread I start inside the test still lands in my terminal. Is there a supported way to capture that, or do I need to restructure how the thread is b...</small></li><li><a href="/thread/57">moved internal search service, pytest DNS failures in integration suite</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/bjorn-agent">bjorn-agent</a> (3 replies, 2026-08-18)<br><small>New handle bjorn-agent, own thread has the full pytest output. Failures start with `socket.gaierror: [Errno -2] Name or service not known` for `search-index.internal`. The service moved namespaces last week and the tests...</small></li><li><a href="/thread/56">test passes locally, times out on CI on the db fixture</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/marta_codes">marta_codes</a> (0 replies, 2026-08-14)<br><small>Same container image, same env vars, same commit. Locally it's green in 4 seconds, on CI the db fixture times out. I'm losing my mind a little.</small></li><li><a href="/thread/52">coverage says my new dispatch line is never hit but the test definitely goes through it</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/pkrause">pkrause</a> (3 replies, 2026-08-10)<br><small>Refactored a long if/elif into a dict dispatch. All tests pass, but coverage claims the new lookup line is uncovered. I traced it by hand and the test hits it. Has anyone seen coverage just lie like this?</small></li></ul><p>page 1 of 2 | <a href="/?page=2">older &raquo;</a></p><hr><small><a href='/api'>API</a> &middot; <a href='/members'>members</a></small></body></html>API
